  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-github",
      "text": "A Source Control and GitHub repository panel for DeepSeek Harness that mirrors the VS Code native Git Source Control view."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **Source Control tab** — a third \"Source Control\" tab in the session view ring (alongside chat and trajectory); when active it fills the main area and splits into the SCM panel (left) and the diff viewer (right) with no overlay, shows only the current session's workspace, and switching back to chat restores the conversation.\n- **Repository header** — repository (workspace) name, current branch, ahead/behind counts, GitHub link, and refresh button.\n- **Commit bar** — multi-line commit message, `Amend` checkbox, `Commit` button with a dropdown (Commit / Commit & Push / Commit & Sync / Undo Last Commit), and a round Sync/Publish button with ↑n ↓n counts.\n- **Change groups** — STAGED CHANGES / CHANGES / MERGE CHANGES (untracked files live inside CHANGES), collapsible, with count badges and group actions (+ stage all / − unstage all / ↶ discard all). File status badges use VS Code colors: `A` green, `M` brown-yellow, `D` red, `R`/`C` blue, `U` green, `!` yellow.\n- **Diff viewer** — side-by-side and inline modes with line numbers and added/removed coloring; the file header shows old path → new path. Conflict files expose Accept Current / Accept Incoming / Accept Both.\n- **Discard with "
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "The plugin uses the repository's normal local Git configuration, SSH keys, HTTPS credential helpers, and Git remotes. It does not call the GitHub API, store GitHub tokens, implement OAuth, depend on GitHub CLI, or expose arbitrary shell commands. GitHub links open the corresponding browser pages; the Compare page is the handoff for creating a pull request. Git writes require an explicit user action, and repository state is reloaded after each operation."
    },
    {
      "section": "Design notes",
      "text": "See [docs/ANALYSIS.md](docs/ANALYSIS.md) for the state model, VS Code Git alignment, local authentication boundary, and GitHub browser handoff design. The panel's visual design follows the DeepSeek design spec — see [docs/UI_DESIGN.md](docs/UI_DESIGN.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- DeepSeek Harness `>=0.1.0-rc.6`\n- Git available on `PATH`\n- A configured Git remote and credential helper for push/fetch/pull operations"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install from a local checkout",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm install\npnpm run build\ndsh plugin --profile web add .\n```\n\nRestart the Web Harness after rebuilding the plugin. A third \"Source Control\" tab appears in the session view ring (next to chat and trajectory)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "- Node.js `>= 22.19`\n- pnpm `>= 9`\n\n```sh\npnpm run check\n```\n\n`pnpm run check` runs `typecheck`, `lint`, `test`, and `build`. CI runs the same command after `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`."
    }
  ],
